                <pb facs="0290" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/60: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the American Delegation to the
                        General Disarmament Conference (Gibson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-02T22:00:00+01:00">February 2, 1932—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 2—9:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. From Wilson. Gilbert’s 69, February 2, 2 p.m.<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d201-f1"/>
                    Drummond has received reply from Shanghai
                    which omits the names of members of Commission but states that first meeting was
                    held this afternoon and that all members are Consuls General and that Italian is
                    also Chargé d’Affaires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
